{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "007S", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fed84a84a3d218d47e6833cd9c389817c7249fba9245fcef9a6504df8738a1e0", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIt follows that in the category of sheaves of sets\nthe notions epimorphism and monomorphism can be described\nas follows.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fee894e39e41e43e710cecfb1feb4f0de364bba4d384f4dd32dc9a840b01b9ef", "unit_id": "tag:007S:prose-0002"}
